                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237970528",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198040324142",
                            "num_reviews": 16,
                            "playtime_forever": 477,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 465,
                            "last_played": 1792275595
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let me just say this first a foremost, IF YOU ARE LOOKING FOR BIG BOSS BATTLES AND NOTHING ELSE, DO NOT PLAY THIS GAME\n\nI swear half the reviews on this page that have something negative to say all complain about either traveling, fighting overworld enemies, the survival mechanics, having to prep for a boss etc etc.\n\nHere's what this game is truly about\nAmazing Environment\nLots to find while exploring\nUpgrading your equipment\nAmazing Boss Fights\nEnvironmental story telling (find notes, look at painting, the shape of areas etc.)\nScavenging for food\nWarmth,Food,Health and sleep management.\n4 Enemy difficulties\n3 Survival difficulties\nMinibosses\n4 sets of armor (starting and find 3)\nSemi respawning loot (loot only respawned once across my entire playthrough so i had to only use what i really needed otherwise the further runs going the same direction would be basically impossible)\n\nHonestly this game shines on the harder difficulties. I played it first time on Hard/Survival and died maybe 3 times across the game. Its not like its that difficult but you 100% cant just rambo through the game either. My only gripe with the game is how often your character gets ragdolled and how sometimes you'll get hit by an AoE that didn't seem like it reached you.  Honest opinion, if you love shadow of the collosus but also love some difficulty mixed in, This is the game for you. Solid 8/10.",
